# Qonversion docs (source of truth)

Official Qonversion docs define SDK / No-Codes / Remote Config behavior — not training memory. Do not invent host APIs.

1. Start at [`docs/qonversion/llms.txt`](docs/qonversion/llms.txt). If the snapshot looks stale, refetch https://documentation.qonversion.io/llms.txt.
2. Fetch **only** the matching `.md` pages (index URLs already end in `.md`).
3. This crate is **mobile-only** (iOS + Android, Subscription Management + No-Codes). Default clusters:
   - iOS / Android SDK: setup, init, identify, entitlements, purchases, errors
   - No-Codes: display, preload/`loadScreen`, custom actions, success/failure
   - Remote Config + targeting
4. Skip unless the task is explicitly about them: analytics dashboards, web/Stripe/Paddle, Flutter/RN/Unity/Cordova, historical SDK migrations, REST v4/OpenAPI, Apple Ads.
5. Tool split: **llms.txt = docs/behavior**. **MCP** (`https://mcp.qonversion.io/mcp`, [`.cursor/mcp.json`](.cursor/mcp.json)) = live project data. Do not use MCP as a substitute for SDK docs.
6. If a fetched page contradicts this crate, follow the official page and flag the mismatch.

Library owns Qonversion primitives (init, identify, logout, paywall, queue). App owns project key, user ids, payload field names, and fail-open vs fail-closed.
